WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.468
Former President Trump filing

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:03.303
a motion seeking to block

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:03.870
former Vice

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.738
President Mike Pence

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:06.873
from speaking to a grand jury

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.141
about efforts to overturn

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.275
the results of the 2020

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.143
presidential election.

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.077
Trump claims

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.612
that the issues are protected

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.314
by executive privilege.

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:14.647
Let's go now

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:15.515
to CNN's Caitlin Paul

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.649
and she joins us now.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.151
Good morning to you, Caitlin.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.387
Realistically, will Trump get his way?

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:23.857
Well, we'll have to see, Don.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.558
Right now, this filing is under seal,

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.127
but this is the third time

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:27.961
that Donald Trump

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:29.295
has tried to make a claim

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:30.663
like this under seal

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:31.931
in this investigation,

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:32.899
trying to claim

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:35.068
that his presidential communications

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:36.603
should be secret

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.304
from criminal investigators.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:39.706
Looking at January six.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.608
And there's a long history here.

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:42.909
Whenever you look back,

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.010
not just

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:44.411
in the

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.246
history of the United States,

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.782
where courts have really not ruled

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:49.382
in favor

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:49.949
of executive

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:50.884
privilege, claims

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.452
whenever there's criminal investigators

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:53.987
wanting to get information.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:55.155
But there's a long history,

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:56.723
even before this judge

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.591
in this particular investigation

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.160
related to January six,

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.895
where Donald Trump has lost

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.329
now every time

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:03.797
he's tried

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:05.865
to make this claim that we know of.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.934
And so it is very possible

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:08.701
he could lose again.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:09.069
It does

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:09.669
make it a little bit

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:10.770
different that this is about

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.538
a communication

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.573
between the vice president

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.408
and the former president himself

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.277
while they're both in office.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.511
But, Don, on the whole,

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:19.412
executive privilege

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.880
does tend to fall away

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.582
whenever a criminal investigator

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:25.151
says we really want an answer here.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:25.885
Caitlin,

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.520
the top Republican and Democrat

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.021
on the House

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:28.755
Intelligence Committee

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:29.789
told Meet the Press

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:30.857
that they have gotten, quote,

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:32.125
a flavor

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.160
of the contents of classified documents

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.429
obtained from Trump, Biden and Pence.

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.097
Listen to this.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:39.833
Right now,

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:40.233
you have

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.501
no idea

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:44.037
whether these were the highest level.

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:46.573
We didn't say we didn't say no. Okay.

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.408
Again, we can't get too into the details

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:51.411
we got a flavor for what was there.

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.012
And I won't speak for Mike,

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:53.780
but I will tell you, having

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:54.848
been given a flavor,

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.616
this is a very serious issue.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:58.084
This wasn't stuff that we can say

00:01:58.084 --> 00:01:59.352
clearly does not matter.

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.721
It matters in all three levels.

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:05.358
Again, we don't we don't know yet.

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:08.128
The question is, what's the flavor?

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:10.263
Well, the flavor is it's not.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:11.397
It's not the whole thing.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.800
It's a taste of what it is.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.702
They clearly are saying that they believe

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:17.070
that there is a serious issue

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.339
here as intelligence committee members,

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:20.740
a Republican

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:21.441
and a Democrat,

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:22.075
standing together

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:23.376
and speaking about what they've learned

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:25.245
in this first crucial briefing.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:26.513
But they are also

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:27.947
in the rest of that interview

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.983
indicating that they are not satisfied

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:31.351
with the amount of information

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:32.886
that they have gotten so far

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:35.054
about these classified documents issues.

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:36.956
They also say that they don't know

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.391
the classification levels

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:40.059
of the documents

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.761
that were being kept outside

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.563
of secure facilities

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.198
in any of these investigations.

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:45.965
And they indicate that

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:48.168
the FBI investigation is ongoing.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.303
At least with Donald Trump.

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.804
We also know that it's ongoing

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.273
with with Joe Biden there.

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:54.073
Special counsel's

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:55.708
looking at both of those things.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.010
And whatever the FBI

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.245
and the intelligence community finds,

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.847
how secure these documents were,

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:01.681
how they were being kept,

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.183
who may have looked at them after

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:04.851
they were outside of the

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:06.419
the hands of the federal government.

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:08.054
All of that is going to play into

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:09.289
charging decisions

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:10.890
and the criminal investigations.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.491
Don, I'm

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:11.958
not sure

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:12.992
if it's going to be in the background

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:13.993
may actually overshadow

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.628
what happens in 20, 24.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.397
Kaitlan, thank you.

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:18.031
Joining us now

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.165
Ellie Honig, CNN senior

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.700
legal analyst, former assistant U.S.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.901
attorney for the Southern District

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.036
of New York.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.605
Ali, we've talked about this

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:26.439
defense before.

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:27.106
Trump has used it

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:27.840
to attempt

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.242
to block or block the testimony

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:31.044
of a number of folks who work for him.

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.478
Does executive privilege

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:33.379
apply to the vice

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.014
president's testimony in this case?

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:38.618
Well, this is a serious long Jim.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:39.118
Donald Trump

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.587
actually has quite a poor record

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:42.088
of winning on these claims.

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:43.022
But he does bring them

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.958
and he does manage to drag things out.

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:45.425
Donald Trump's

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:46.826
got two big problems

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:48.027
with his executive privilege

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.062
argument here.

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:50.063
The first one is that

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.998
this is a criminal grand jury subpoena.

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:54.100
And courts tend to honor and uphold

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.201
grand jury subpoenas,

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.169
not automatically,

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:57.537
but typically a grand jury subpoena

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:58.371
will overcome

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.806
a claim of executive privilege.

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:00.840
The second problem is Donald

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.709
Trump is not president anymore.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:04.043
He's a former president.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:05.311
Again, it's possible

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.246
that a former president

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:08.047
can bring in executive privilege claim,

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:09.182
but it's much more difficult

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:09.916
than if he were still

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:10.683
the sitting president.

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.418
So I think this one's a long shot.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.519
But as you said, Jim,

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:14.821
this is a pattern for Donald Trump.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.589
He likes to claim executive privilege.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.691
It helps him slow things down.

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.026
Look, I think everybody knew

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.561
this was coming, right?

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:22.562
We know that Mike Pence

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.330
is also trying to claim that

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.099
under the speech and debate clause

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:27.767
that he doesn't need

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.202
to submit to the subpoena.

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:30.870
When you look at where we stand,

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.505
do you see a scenario

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:33.773
where the special counsel

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:34.607
moves forward

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.776
without Mike Pence's testimony?

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:39.579
so that's a really interesting

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:40.346
question, Erica.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:41.414
And that's the calculation

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:42.949
that that special counsel

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:43.916
has to make right now.

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:45.285
Do we go to court and fight

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:46.185
both of these claims?

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:46.686
Donald Trump's

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:47.520
executive privilege,

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.888
plain and Mike Pence's

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:49.956
speech and debate claim?

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.391
Do we take it through the district court?

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:52.759
Do we go to the court of appeals?

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:53.426
If we
when do we

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:54.727
maybe then have to wait

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:55.495
for the Supreme Court

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:56.763
or do we just move ahead

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.131
without Mike Pence's testimony?

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.132
But here's the risk.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.301
You need to know what Mike Pence says.

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:02.435
If you're a prosecutor,

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:03.970
A, it could be helpful to your case.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:04.470
There were certain

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.571
one on one conversations

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:06.739
you would want to know about

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:07.674
he might be harmful.

00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:09.042
What if Mike Pence went in there

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:09.642
and said things

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.311
that were all favorable to Donald Trump?

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.345
What if Mike Pence said

00:05:12.345 --> 00:05:13.246
he never pressured me?

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:15.148
He told me to just do the right thing.

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:16.649
You need to know that either way

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:17.550
as a prosecutor,

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:19.652
we will be

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:21.421
watching and waiting and calling on you

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:22.955
as always, for your expertize.

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:24.090
Lee, thank you.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.525
Always ready, guys. Thank you.

